# QGroundControl Takeoff Implementation

## Working Takeoff Pattern

### Mission Structure
```cpp
// Item 0: Home position (deleted by system)
MissionItem* homeItem = new MissionItem(0, MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT, 
                                       0, 0, 0, 0, homeLat, homeLng, 0, false, false, parent);

// Item 1: Takeoff (first real mission item)
MissionItem* takeoffItem = new MissionItem(1, MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT,
                                          0, 0, 0, 0, takeoffLat, takeoffLng, takeoffAlt, false, false, parent);

// Item 2+: Waypoints
MissionItem* waypointItem = new MissionItem(2, MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT,
                                           0, 0, 0, 0, wpLat, wpLng, wpAlt, false, false, parent);

// Item N: Land
MissionItem* landItem = new MissionItem(n, MAV_CMD_NAV_LAND, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT,
                                       0, 0, 0, 0, landLat, landLng, 0, false, false, parent);
```

### Complete Implementation Example
```cpp
void MissionUploadService::uploadMissionToVehicle(Vehicle* vehicle, const QList<QGeoCoordinate>& waypoints, int altitude)
{
    if (!vehicle || !vehicle->missionManager() || waypoints.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }
    
    QGeoCoordinate droneCurrentPosition = vehicle->coordinate();
    if (!droneCurrentPosition.isValid()) {
        return;
    }
    
    QList<MissionItem*> missionItems;
    QObject* missionItemParent = vehicle;
    
    // 1. Home position (will be deleted by system)
    QGeoCoordinate homeCoord = droneCurrentPosition;
    homeCoord.setAltitude(0);
    MissionItem* homeItem = new MissionItem(0, MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT, 
                                           0, 0, 0, 0, homeCoord.latitude(), homeCoord.longitude(), homeCoord.altitude(), 
                                           false, false, missionItemParent);
    missionItems.append(homeItem);
    
    // 2. Takeoff (first real mission item)
    QGeoCoordinate takeoffCoord = droneCurrentPosition;
    takeoffCoord.setAltitude(altitude);
    MissionItem* takeoffItem = new MissionItem(1, MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT, 
                                              0, 0, 0, 0, takeoffCoord.latitude(), takeoffCoord.longitude(), takeoffCoord.altitude(), 
                                              false, false, missionItemParent);
    missionItems.append(takeoffItem);
    
    // 3. Waypoints
    for (int i = 0; i < waypoints.size(); i++) {
        QGeoCoordinate coord = waypoints[i];
        coord.setAltitude(altitude);
        MissionItem* waypointItem = new MissionItem(i + 2, MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT,
                                                   0, 0, 0, 0, coord.latitude(), coord.longitude(), coord.altitude(), 
                                                   false, false, missionItemParent);
        missionItems.append(waypointItem);
    }
    
    // 4. Land
    QGeoCoordinate landCoord = droneCurrentPosition;
    landCoord.setAltitude(0);
    MissionItem* landItem = new MissionItem(waypoints.size() + 2, MAV_CMD_NAV_LAND, MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT,
                                           0, 0, 0, 0, landCoord.latitude(), landCoord.longitude(), landCoord.altitude(), 
                                           false, false, missionItemParent);
    missionItems.append(landItem);
    
    // 5. Upload
    vehicle->missionManager()->writeMissionItems(missionItems);
}
```

## Key Points

### Why This Works
- **Home position as item 0**: Gets deleted by QGroundControl's safety logic
- **Takeoff as item 1**: Becomes the first real mission item sent to vehicle
- **Sequential numbering**: Required for proper mission execution
- **Proper coordinate storage**: Uses param5/6/7 for lat/lng/alt

### Common Mistakes
- ❌ Putting takeoff as first item (gets deleted)
- ❌ Skipping home position (causes issues)
- ❌ Wrong sequence numbering
- ❌ Using setCoordinate() instead of constructor parameters

### Debugging
- Always log complete mission before upload
- Verify takeoff appears as item 1 in logs
- Check that home position is item 0 (will be deleted)
- Confirm proper coordinate values in param5/6/7

## Mission Types

### Regular Mission
- Home → Takeoff → Waypoints → Land
- Used for standard flight missions

### Loiter Mission  
- Home → Takeoff → Loiter → Land
- Used for observation/patrol missions

### Both patterns follow the same structure with different middle items